commands provided by MCP server on tools:
tools/list
tools/describe
tools/call

test in Postman:
File -> New -> MCP (MCP request is better than HTTP request)
copy path of server.js in VScode and paste in Postman url field, click Connect, grant STDIO access to 'All requests in this workspace' in popup winodw
click 'get_current_weather' API, fill in latitude and longitude, click Run, Json response body shows up as expected
an alternative way to call that API:
in terminal: $ curl "https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=45.4318&longitude=-123.1416&hourly=temperature_2m,relativehumidity_2m"

tie Claude to MCP server: add the chunk below to claude_desktop_config.json
  "mcpServers": {
    "Weather Service": {
      "command": "/usr/local/bin/node",
      "args": ["/Users/lilywu/github/Weather-MCP-Server/server.js"]
    }
  }
re-open Claude -> Connectors, it would show "Weather Service" enabled.
then ask "whats the weather in Forest Grove, Oregon today?", it would auto fill in the parameters like latitude and longitude, etc. (easier than manually fill in Postman)
so in this way, we've built a local MCP server which can communicate with an API, mixing Claude LLM capabilities with this API's real-time capabilities (since LLM has a cutoff time)

3 protocols of setting up MCP servers:
STDIO: local
HTTPS
SSE: Server Sent Event, persistent connection



difference of MCP request and HTTP request:
HTTP API:
┌─────────────┐
│ AI Agent    │
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       │ "I need weather data"
       ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ AI must know:       │
│                     │
│ URL                 │
│ HTTP method         │
│ Parameters          │
│ Authentication      │
│ Response format     │
└──────────┬──────────┘
           │
           │ HTTP request
           ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Weather API         │
└─────────────────────┘

MCP server:
┌─────────────┐
│ AI Agent    │
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼
┌─────────────┐
│ MCP Client  │
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       │ "What tools are available?"
       ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│ MCP Server      │
│                 │
│ get_weather()   │
│ search_user()   │
│ get_orders()    │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         │ Tool information
         ▼
┌──────────────┐
│ AI / LLM     │
│              │
│ "I need      │
│ get_weather" │
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       │ MCP tool call
       ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│ MCP Server      │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         │ HTTP / API
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│ Weather API     │
└─────────────────┘

MCP does NOT replace HTTP, HTTP could be still used behind the MCP Server.






